    <!--
      To publish a new release:
      1. Update VERSION in packaging/Resistine.spec
      2. Build the DMG with ./scripts/build/build-distribution.sh
      3. Sign the DMG:  ./vpn-apple/Sparkle.framework/Resources/bin/sign_update dist/Resistine-Installer.dmg
      4. Add a new <item> with the version, signature, length, and download URL
      5. Push this file + the DMG to resistine.github.io

      IMPORTANT: sparkle:version MUST match CFBundleVersion in the app inside
      the DMG, otherwise Sparkle will re-download the same update endlessly.

      Linux releases use sparkle:os="linux" on the enclosure so the Linux
      updater can filter for its platform. Example:

        <item>
          <title>Version 2026.03.24</title>
          <description><![CDATA[
            <h2>What's New</h2>
            <ul><li>Linux auto-updater support</li></ul>
          ]]></description>
          <pubDate>Mon, 24 Mar 2026 12:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
          <enclosure
            url="https://resistine.github.io/releases/linux/Resistine-Desktop-2026.03.24-linux.tar.gz"
            sparkle:version="2026.03.24"
            sparkle:shortVersionString="2026.03.24"
            length="15000000"
            type="application/gzip"
            sparkle:edSignature="BASE64_ED25519_SIGNATURE"
            sparkle:os="linux"
          />
        </item>

      To sign a Linux tarball, use the same Ed25519 key pair as macOS:
        python3 -c "
        import base64, sys
        from cryptography.hazmat.primitives.asymmetric.ed25519 import Ed25519PrivateKey
        key = Ed25519PrivateKey.from_private_bytes(base64.b64decode(sys.argv[1]))
        data = open(sys.argv[2], 'rb').read()
        print(base64.b64encode(key.sign(data)).decode())
        " PRIVATE_KEY_B64 path/to/archive.tar.gz
    -->

